+// Records Qwen3.6 MoE routing: which experts each token's router picked (ffn_moe_topk)
+// and each pick's raw softmax probability (ffn_moe_weights), before the later top-k
+// renormalization. Both nodes appear once per decoder layer per microbatch:
+//   ffn_moe_topk-N     I32 [n_expert_used, n_tokens] - a strided VIEW of the full
+//                      argsort: element stride nb[0], row stride nb[1] spans all
+//                      n_expert entries, so only the first k elements of each row
+//                      belong to the top-k.
+//   ffn_moe_weights-N  F32 [1, n_expert_used, n_tokens] - rank r of token tok lives
+//                      at byte offset tok*nb[2] + r*nb[1].
+// Reads honor the strides. topk and weights of the same (layer, microbatch) are
